    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class; the other two files are an abstract base and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `selfLink` field so that a created owner reports `'/api/owners/' + id`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` read-only property to the `Owner` schema (in the `allOf` block alongside `id`/`displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `selfLink` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` and a small `selfLink(Owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (or `null` before an id is assigned).\n\n**Placement rationale:** The existing pattern puts pure domain-derived values (salutation, locality, timezone\u2026) as getters on the `Owner` entity, while values that encode an API-presentation concern (`displayName`, `telephoneDisplay`) live as mapper expressions in the REST layer. `selfLink` embeds the API path (`/api/owners/`), which is a REST/HATEOAS concern rather than a domain fact \u2014 so it belongs in the mapper next to the other presentation mappings, keeping the entity free of URL knowledge and reusing the established expression-mapping approach rather than duplicating logic.",
